Implemented [2.py](/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/fable/6/017/2.py). `main(input_grid)` parses grey contiguous spans on the top row and left column, uses each colored singleton only if it lies inside a valid row-span/column-span intersection, paints that full rectangle in the singleton’s color, and otherwise clears shadows and distractors to background.

I also added `generate_input()` to produce varied valid ARC instances with reusable projections and out-of-intersection distractor dots. A self-check loop loaded the module, ran `generate_input()+main()` 120 times, and verified `ndarray`/2D/size constraints plus semantic agreement with an independent checker.
